    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d726">

                <pb facs="0818" n="730" xml:id="pg730"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. McCormick to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1904-05-21"><hi rendition="#italic">May 21,
                        1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 141.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose to you herewith
                    a copy of Law Bulletin No. 65, of April 23, 1904, containing, under the No. 744,
                    the ukase of His Majesty the Emperor placing cotton among the articles
                    imperially declared on February 14/27 to be contraband of war.</p>
                <p>As I have already cabled, the customs authorities informed me, in answer to
                    inquiry made of them, that this decree applied to raw cotton. I have asked
                    through the foreign office that this information be transmitted’ to me
                    officially, and I have no reason to believe that such official information will
                    be other than that furnished to me in response to the inquiry above alluded
                    to.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert S.
                    McCormick.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d726-a1.xml" xpointer="d726-a1"/>
            </div>
